In Merge, we need to perform multiple time merge if the project is very active
Suppose master branch is very active and other branch work is still ongoing then
merge approach performs lot of commit.

Rebasing!

> We can instead rebase the <branch-name> branch onto the master branch.
  This moves the entire <branch-name> so that it BEGINS at the tip of the master
  branch. All of the work is still there, but we have re-written history.

> Instead of using a merge commit, rebasing rewrites history
  by creating new commits for each of the original <branch-name> commits.

> git switch <branch-name>
> git rebase master
